le endpoint, evolves by adding fields (not versions). But the N+1 query problem is real, caching requires work (custom layers), and you need resolver logic to prevent malicious queries from hammering your DB.\n\n**Main tradeoff**: REST is simpler to build, GraphQL is simpler to consume at scale. Pick REST unless your API serves many clients with conflicting data needs or you're already managing a fleet of backend services. GraphQL shines when you have a mobile client, web app, and third-party integrations all using the same data differently.","ttft_ms":3958,"type":"result","duration_ms":6530,"uuid":"f8b97713-fb46-42d5-8721-a8028390de3f","ttft_stream_ms":1331,"time_to_request_ms":120,"first_content_frame_ms":1331,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":429,"cacheReadInputTokens":7913,"cacheCreationInputTokens":524,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0039943,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":225,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":524,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-12T05:14:51.381Z"}